  cached for the ends of a range), the wait/wake pattern PianoPower's PianoAdsp.cpp waitEvents.

New here (UniXNU-piano): PianoSensors.cpp (the kext: levels 1-4 on PianoPower's client contract), SensorsGuard.c/.h (the safety
governor), SensorsHealth.h (PianoPower's health report as the guard's observation), SensorsPolicy.c/.h (piano's facts, the arena check,
the light curve, the rotation policy), SensorsClient.c/.h (level 3's SNS client: lookups and attributes), SensorsStream.c/.h (level 4's
streams), SensorsLoad.c/.h (the pack from the ESP), SensorsAddon.c/.h and tools/sensor_addon.py (the pack carried by a RAM test
image), tests/piano.c, tests/bringup.c, tests/streams.c, tests/load.c and tests/addon.c (their tests and the independent cross-checks),
tests/qrtr_frame.h, tests/run-host-tests.py.

UniXNU's boot addon, as a format only (no code taken): the container layout of UniXNU's scripts/make-gpu-addon.py ("NGPUADD2", the
count, the total, per file its path, mode, size, compressed size, the path and the zlib stream padded to 8 bytes) and DarwinBoot's
handling of Payloads/<kernel>.gpuaddon (DarwinBootPkg/Driver/DarwinBoot.c: the /chosen/memory-map GpuAddon slot, the header checked,
the file copied into the kernel's memory); the kext inflates the entry with libkern's zlib (inflateInit_, inflate, inflateEnd).

This repository's own code compiled in from its package (not copied): package/PianoAuto/AutoStream.c/.h (a stream's off/on rules) and
AutoLight.c/.h (the light chain over SensorsPolicy's ps_als_step), linked into the kext for level 4; their tests run before the build.

Specification only, no code or text taken (facts as in docs/drivers/sensors.md sections 3 and 5c): Linux drivers/misc/fastrpc.c and the
SM8750 devicetree (GPL-2.0, the piano kernel tree v1.1.0); linux-msm/hexagonrpc 598b591a and the Ubuntu project's seven patches to it
(LGPL-3.0 / GPL-3.0); libssc 54dd13e3 (GPL-3.0): its protos' message ids and fields, its enable (514 on change, 513 with a rate) and
disable (10) requests, one QMI client per sensor; iio-sensor-proxy 3.9 (GPL-3.0); libqmi's SSC service description (LGPL-2.1); Android's
sensor reporting modes (the light on change, the accelerometer continuous) and its sensors HAL's one client per sensor, as behaviour.
qualcomm/fastrpc v1.0.7 (BSD-3-Clause) was read for its IDL's handle, method and argument numbers; no code was taken from it either.
